WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Your player has crossed the finish line.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:10.000
How do you make sure their hard-earned win gets the recognition it deserves?

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Your final act as a Player-Coach is to facilitate the championship conversation.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.000
And the first part of it is about amplifying their success.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.000
This has two parts.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Celebrate publicly to reinforce the value of development

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.000
and provide visibility to act as their sponsor and advocate.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:39.000
A manager sent a team-wide email celebrating her player's completion of the program

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.000
and highlighting a specific project where she applied her new skills.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Then she scheduled a 15-minute coffee with her own boss and the player

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:55.000
simply to say, I want you to hear about the great work Sarah is doing.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.000
That visibility is priceless.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Your play is twofold.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.000
First, use the template in your playbook to send a recognition note.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Second, identify one senior leader who should hear about your player's success

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.000
and plan how you'll create that connection.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Your player is humble and uncomfortable with public praise.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.000
How do you celebrate their success in a way

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.000
that feels authentic and respectful to them

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.000
while still providing the visibility they've earned?

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:31.000
It's an opportunity to learn how they like to be recognized and rewarded.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.000
For some, it's a public praise. For others, it's private acknowledgement.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.000
While others prefer financial recognition or new opportunities.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.935
Through understanding more about your player's M.V.P.,

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:44.000
you can build an authentic connection.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:49.000
The Authentic Recognition Guide in your playbook offers strategies

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:53.000
for tailoring your celebration to your player style.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:58.000
In our final segment, we'll discuss how to frame this victory

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.000
as the beginning of their next season of growth.
